[B][SIZE=6]Project Gielinor — Native Rust OSRS 239.1 Client[/SIZE][/B]

Hi everyone! We have been building an OSRS 239.1 client in Rust. It runs without Java. This thread follows it from the first bits of terrain to the client we have running now. There is still plenty to finish.

The live screenshots use our local Kotlin test server. Other pictures come from renderer or interface tests, and are labeled so you can tell them apart.

[B][SIZE=4]Where things stand[/SIZE][/B]

Here is the breakdown from the 18 October parity log. Each number is a tracked behavior, not a whole feature or a percentage of the client.

Matched means the recorded checks agree with Java. Partial means there is more to finish or test. Needs checking means the code is there, but the full behavior has not been verified. Unclassified means we still need to work out the coverage.

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Area[/TH][TH]Matched[/TH][TH]Partial[/TH][TH]Needs checking[/TH][TH]Unclassified[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Login and sessions[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]3[/TD][TD]6[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Networking[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]3[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Cache and assets[/TD][TD]4[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]1[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Terrain, scenes and rendering[/TD][TD]32[/TD][TD]8[/TD][TD]7[/TD][TD]2[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Actors and animation[/TD][TD]7[/TD][TD]2[/TD][TD]5[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Child worlds[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]2[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Scripts and text[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]7[/TD][TD]4[/TD][TD]1[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Widgets and interfaces[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]11[/TD][TD]7[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Inventory and gameplay state[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]3[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Movement and interactions[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]2[/TD][TD]3[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]World map and minimap[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]2[/TD][TD]3[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Sound and music[/TD][TD]2[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]4[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Windowing and input[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]2[/TD][TD]4[/TD][TD]1[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Social and saved settings[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]6[/TD][TD]0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Test setup and acceptance[/TD][TD]1[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]0[/TD][TD]1[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Total: 155[/B][/TD][TD][B]50[/B][/TD][TD][B]44[/B][/TD][TD][B]55[/B][/TD][TD][B]6[/B][/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

Banking, longer combat sessions, reconnects, world hopping and proper scene occlusion still need work. A working screen or a passing test does not close those out.

[B]Some concrete results from the log[/B]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Check[/TH][TH]Recorded result[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Packet IDs and lengths[/TD][TD]149 incoming + 117 outgoing declarations match Java. Packet behavior is tracked separately.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Incoming packet behavior[/TD][TD]27 partial, 119 implemented but not fully verified, 2 unclassified, 1 missing (reflection checks).[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Outgoing packet behavior[/TD][TD]1 partial, 1 implemented but not fully verified, 115 still awaiting full audit.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Terrain/model drawing order[/TD][TD]128 controlled images matched Java pixel for pixel. This is a small renderer test, not a full game frame.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Ground-item tile lifetime[/TD][TD]512 packet transitions, 128 item-layer lifecycles and 128 bridge-terrain lifecycles checked against Java.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Latest regression run[/TD][TD]1,111 tests passed across 566 suites; one old approximation test remains ignored.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Latest native run[/TD][TD]819 frames, 3 server-confirmed actions and 0 audio errors. Longer play sessions still need testing.[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

These counts come from the behavior checklist. The larger method, module and script-candidate inventories are still being reviewed and are not included in the 155. The numbers will change as that work is broken down. [URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/main/threads/client-project-parity-log.json]Checkpoint counts and requirement IDs[/URL]

